text:
@JakeInMotion Hey Jake, I tried as you said. I selected the position property, but it still didn't apply any expression. 
Although it created two sliders in the effects panel of the layer. One for frequency, one for amplitude. Looks like the expression is not applied somehow
Maybe it's my mac 😌

@mobiltec Indeed, while I wasn't a creator in the early days, I remember that the whole idea of YouTube is that is was "the tube" (TV) produced by you. Now, many of the most successful channels have entire production staffs...writers, camera operators, sound guys, editors, talent. It has looped around to become what it was originally shunning.

On the flip side, the opportunity for small independent creators like me to earn a little income from the work is the only way it was possible for me to devote the time needed to film and edit my videos. But it absolutely has turned into a mad competition for ad revenue, where quality, useful content gets beat out by sensational & eye-catching but ultimately hollow content.

It's frustrating that I know in advance that my best work with beautiful footage, carefully crafted soundtrack and thoughtful commentary will always be outperformed by my less-well-made episodes where something happens to go wrong...strife always seems to drive clicks, but I don't like it when stuff going wrong. 😆 Thank you for watching & commenting!

@stoopidhoomons But it's already smarter than 99% of people... It does not matter if people consider it "A.I." or not.

EDIT
Also, this is just the beginning (like the internet in 1990).

@Paulolz22 Last time I read about that terrible plan it was a request from the US military that was rejected by Taiwan. On the grounds that even if the factories got taken they wouldn't be able to operate it. 

Lets suppose it was put in place.
Invasion occurs. Explosions triggered. Invasion repelled. Now what? Keep in mind that 40%+ of the economy was blown up on top of whatever other damage occurred due to the fighting.

@codetaku7 TSMC relies on a Dutch company,  ASML which makes the machines that make the chips. ASML relies on ZEISS a German company that makes the highly accurate mirrors for EV (extreme ultra-violet), which go into the machine. 

There's a lot of 'one building the world relies on' in the supply chain for advanced semi-conductors. All of them have co-ordinates already set in missiles owned by China and Russia should they ever want to take them out.

Western governments are not taking this seriously because it would cost too much to pay for duplicate manufacturing facilities, "just in case". Western governments can't afford it because it would require taxing rich people, which is forbidden as they're owned by rich people.

@nigelmakesgames Thanks for sharing your experience. There might be a misunderstanding in the use of the word "discomfort." By no means do we want people to suffer or approach something in "the only right way" and end up feeling incompetent or incapable. Like with stress, there is good difficulty and bad difficulty. Just like you said "until it clicks" but when it's not clicking, it's likely because something isn't clear and is thus "challenge" or "not straightforward" which means the person needs to overcome that. 

This could be a fun process at times, but fun doesn't mean without friction.

What do you think of this framing?

@natiworku4250 There's NOTHING to "learn" about AI! That's the damn point! You just use it! Even idiots don't have to learn AI! They just use it!

Anyway, I am currently using it as a Coding Buddy! And I'm happy to let AI write corporate wank for me! Like work emails, CVs, formal letters etc! Stuff that doesn't require a working brain to do!

But I'm STILL going to code though! Because I Bloody Enjoy It!!! I don't give a flying F what other people do! I have a RIGHT to do what I enjoy! End of!

@jeremielebrun3637 psychopaths do have goals. We have more successful business owners with anti social personality disorder than we do inmates. They do incredibly well in our society because they have no feelings towards the well being of others. They influence people, highly emotionally intelligent, the world’s a stage and they are great actors. Hard to control because they’ll manipulate you into thinking you’re in control.

Sure, you can get leverage over anyone, but at least the psychopath isn’t making choices purely out of the love of the game and only hurts those that are threats or just collateral damage. 

Very often you get a sadistic psycho tho as these guys do have emotions. Just not the same as us. Nobody is void of any feelings. They are masters of emotions and not lead by them. It’s just unusual for a human to operate like that.
